; C13c  Winning 42 p. 49 (W42-p049-c); the 84 form is pp. 70-72 (W42-p070-b,
; W42-p071-b); played in Hand 35, p. 117 (W42-p117-b)
; Rule, in our words: a setter following a suit in which he holds exactly two
; tiles, neither of them count, plays the lower and keeps the higher.
; Python gate (pour_setter gate_c13c): a setter following a non-trump lead with
; exactly two followers, neither count; the book's tile is the lower.
; How this encoding differs: it cannot say "exactly two" and, with three or
; more non-count followers, allows every follower some other one outranks.
; With two it is the gate.
; GAP declarer: the bidder is written in as S0 (only to name the setters).
; GAP none: "exactly two followers" needs "no third follower".
(policy c13c-low-from-a-pair
  (initial play)
  (fallback lowest-legal)
  (rule follow-low (in play) (next play) (select answer)
    (guard
      (query
        (roles (chair me) (domino low) (domino high) (context led))
        (out low)
        (pattern
          (viewer me)
          (opponent me S0)
          (led-context led)
          (not (context led q*))
          (own-legal low)
          (in low led)
          (count low 0)
          (own-legal high)
          (in high led)
          (count high 0)
          (beats high low led))))))
